From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:30:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D513 code mode: btoa and atob throw InvalidCharacterError

Upstream: btoa and atob threw a TypeError for invalid input, where JS throws a DOMException named InvalidCharacterError (the WPT-adapted tests checked for TypeError, noting that code mode has no DOMException).
Fixed: they throw an Error named InvalidCharacterError, the closest code mode has to that DOMException (e.name, String(e), instanceof Error, and the uncaught message "InvalidCharacterError: The string contains invalid characters. (line, col)"). The message text is unchanged. A failure can now carry such a name; both engines, and the VM snapshot saves it.
Scenarios: codemode-stdlib-web.test.ts "bytes and text" (btoa invalid, atob invalid)
Upstream tests: test/web-wpt.test.ts checks the InvalidCharacterError name where it checked for TypeError, and adds "invalid input throws an Error named InvalidCharacterError, the DOMException JS throws"

diff --git a/packages/codemode/src/interpreter/errors.ts b/packages/codemode/src/interpreter/errors.ts
index 9699c3b941..815320f3eb 100644
--- a/packages/codemode/src/interpreter/errors.ts
+++ b/packages/codemode/src/interpreter/errors.ts
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ export const normalizeError = (error: unknown): Diagnostic => {
     const location = error.node?.loc ? sourceLocation(error.node) : undefined
     return {
       kind: error.kind,
-      message: `${error.type}: ${error.message}${formatLocation(location)}`,
+      message: `${error.name ?? error.type}: ${error.message}${formatLocation(location)}`,
       ...(location ? { location } : {}),
       ...(error.suggestions ? { suggestions: error.suggestions } : {}),
     }
@@ -124,6 +124,7 @@ export const materialize = <R>(ctx: Interpreter<R>, thrown: unknown): Value => {
   if (thrown instanceof PendingThrow) {
     if (thrown.value === undefined) {
       thrown.value = createErrorValue(builtins[thrown.type], thrown.message)
+      if (thrown.name !== undefined) define(thrown.value, "name", thrown.name, hidden)
       thrown.value.host = thrown
     }
     return thrown.value
